    <summary>Identifies why an operation is unsafe, as reported by <see cref="T:Android.App.Admin.UnsafeStateException" />.</summary>
    <remarks><para><see cref="F:Android.App.Admin.OperationSafetyReason.DrivingDistraction" /> is the only reason that Android makes public. <see cref="M:Android.App.Admin.DevicePolicyManager.IsSafeOperation(System.Int32)" /> and <see cref="M:Android.App.Admin.DeviceAdminReceiver.OnOperationSafetyStateChanged(Android.Content.Context,System.Int32,System.Boolean)" /> use the <see cref="T:System.Int32" /> type for the reason. Cast <see cref="F:Android.App.Admin.OperationSafetyReason.DrivingDistraction" /> when you pass it to <see cref="M:Android.App.Admin.DevicePolicyManager.IsSafeOperation(System.Int32)" />.</para></remarks>
  </Docs>
